            "patch_url": "https://github.com/DirtyHairy/async-mutex/pull/95.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "Cancelling an oversized queued acquire leaves eligible `waitForUnlock` calls pending even though capacity is available. Re-evaluate unlock waiters after clearing the queue, while preserving capacity held by active acquisitions. Bound the scan by registered waiter weights so cancellation also returns promptly for large or unlimited capacity.\n\nFixes #94. Both regression cases failed before the change in the Semaphore and withTimeout suites. All 159 tests now pass with 100% coverage; lint and CJS/ESM builds pass. Rollup reports the existing generated-helper `this` warnings. Tests used Node's `--no-experimental-strip-types` flag so Mocha uses the repository's ts-node compiler; the browser matrix was not run.\n",
